'''Description:''' ([[prestige class|PRESTIGE CLASS]]) The highest art is magic, often referred to as *the* Art. Its most advanced practitioners are frequently archmages, bending spells in ways unavailable to other spellcasters. 

'''[[Hit die]]:'''  d4

'''Proficiencies:''' An archmage does not gain any additional weapon or armor proficiencies. 

'''[[Skill point]]s:''' 2 + [[Int]] mod

'''Skills:''' [[concentration]], [[craft armor]], [[craft weapon]], [[heal (skill)|heal]], [[lore]], [[persuade]], [[search]], [[spellcraft]]

'''[[Saving throw|Primary saving throw(s)]]:''' [[will]]

'''[[Base attack bonus|Base attack bonus progression]]:'''  1 BAB per 2 levels

== Requirements ==

'''Alignment restriction:''' none

'''[[Arcane|Arcane spellcasting]]:'''  Must be able to cast level 7 spells.

'''[[Skill]]s:''' [[spellcraft]] 15 ranks, [[lore]] 15 ranks

'''[[Feat]]s:''' [[skill focus]] (spellcraft), [[spell focus]] (any)

==Special abilities & feats==
*Level 1: [[high arcana]], [[mastery of elements (normal)]]
*Level 2: high arcana
*Level 3: high arcana 
*Level 4: high arcana
*Level 5: high arcana 

== Bonus spells ==

The archmage sacrifices the bonus [[spell slot]]s he should gain in order to take a [[high arcana]] feat at each level. He does, however, add his level to his base caster class when determining spell power (damage, duration...).

==Notes==
*Requires the [[PRC Expansion Pack]].

